# Soma's search, pulled down from home (105+). Bugs from the 135 check on Boss's phone: "dicsord" (two letters
# swapped) didn't find Discord; recent searches never showed when nothing was opened; name searches brought rows of
# unrelated photos. The emulator has no Discord: Chrome and Settings stand in.
# Each pull is checked by the app's own log line (139: a terminal tile that still held the focus made every pull
# open nothing, the Mac Pro's 138 walks). Typing on home is no way in: it searches the app list, not this.
# A clean start: no shade or dialog left by an earlier walk.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
# The Soma keyboard, as on Boss's phone: Gboard autocorrects "chorme" before search sees it (reinstalls reset the IME).
ime dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.keyboard.OmaKeyboardService
key BACK
key HOME
wait 1500
# Home pressed on home opens the app list with its search field and keyboard (as the gesture bar's swipe up does, on
# purpose): one Back puts the keyboard away, a second the list; else the first pull only closed the list (the Mac Pro,
# 139/140). On home already, a Back does nothing.
key BACK
wait 600
key BACK
# Home settled first.
wait 2000
clearlog
# Pull search down from the middle of home.
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
type chorme
wait 1500
expect Chrome
shot typo-finds-chrome
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
# Put away without opening anything: still a recent search.
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
expect Recent searches
expect chorme
shot recent-searches-shown
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
type setitngs
wait 2500
expect Settings
# Look: no row of unrelated photos under Settings.
shot typo-finds-settings-no-photo-noise
key BACK
key BACK
[phone] Tap the terminal tile on home, leave it (Back), then pull search down from the middle of home: it opens with the keyboard, and stays (it did nothing before 139).
[phone] Search "dicsord": Discord comes first, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "andrew" (a contact): the contact with Call/Text, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "beach": his beach and marina photos still show.
[phone] Type a search, put search away without opening anything, pull it down again: the search is under Recent searches.
